{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QReebVectorField","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QReebVectorField","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qReebVectorField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qReebVectorField","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.lean#L44-L56","doc":"**q-Deformed Reeb vector field**: defined by its action on smooth functions\n`ξ_q(f) = q⁻¹ ξ(f) + (1 − q⁻¹) [ξ, X_f]_q`.\n\nHere `xi_f p = ξ(f)(p)` and `bracket_q_xi_Xf p = [ξ, X_f]_q(p)` are the\npointwise values over the ground ring `R_q`, and `q_inv` is the local\nvalue of `q⁻¹` (the image of `q_inv_param` under the substrate\nspecialisation `ι : R_q → R_q`).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-reeb-vector-field}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:q-reeb-vector-field","label":"ex:q-reeb-vector-field","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.lean#L39-L40","doc":"The inverse indeterminate `q⁻¹ = T⁻¹` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The canonical indeterminate `q = T¹` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-reeb-vector-field.lean#L34-L36","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}